# {{PROJECT_NAME}} - Tutorial Hub
# 30 interactive lessons covering JVN from first dialogue line to release checklist.
# Each lesson is a separate .vns file in scripts/tutorial/.
# Lessons are self-contained — the player can take them in any order.
# The tutorial_count variable (set to 0 in the prologue) tracks how many the player completes.
# When the player leaves this hub, the end_early label shows progress-aware feedback.

@scenario {{SCENARIO_PREFIX}}_tutorial_hub
@include {{CHARACTERS_INCLUDE}}

{{BG_DECL}}@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[set ui.textBoxAsset none]
[set ui.continueIndicator spinning_arrow]
[if tutorial_still]
[set ui.reduceMotion true]
[else]
[set ui.reduceMotion false]
[endif]
[if !tutorial_initialized]
[set tutorial_count 0]
[flag tutorial_initialized]
[endif]
[set ui.characterHeightFactor 1.5]
[set ui.characterBaselineY 1.5]
[set character.lavender.imageEffect none]
[textspeed 28]
[autodelay 1700]
[set ui.characterHeightFactor 1.5]
[set ui.characterBaselineY 1.5]
{{BG_START}}
[show lavender center happy]
[wait 200]

Lavender: Welcome! I'm Lavender, your guide through these tutorials.
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: There are {b}30 lessons{/b} ahead. Each one teaches a part of JVN — from writing your first dialogue line to shipping a finished game.

Lavender: Every lesson is a real {b}.vns{/b} file inside {b}scripts/tutorial/{/b}. You can open any of them in the editor right now, side by side with this hub.
Lavender: They're designed to be modified. Change the code, break something, see what happens — that's how the syntax sticks.

[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: The lessons are grouped into six pages. Pick any topic — they're self-contained, so order doesn't matter.
Lavender: Finish a lesson with its return-to-hub option to mark it complete. Replaying it never adds a second completion.
Lavender: The stage is plain white, my drawing stays still, and the translucent textbox keeps our conversation readable.
> Keep the spinning continue arrow -> topics_page_1
> Use a still continue arrow -> set_still

@label set_still
[flag tutorial_still]
[set ui.reduceMotion true]
[set character.lavender.imageEffect none]
[jump topics_page_1]

@label set_motion
[unflag tutorial_still]
[set ui.reduceMotion false]
[set character.lavender.imageEffect none]
[jump topics_page_1]

@label topics_page_1
[show lavender far_left talking]
[wait 120]
Lavender: Writing and presenting — how text, characters, and visuals reach the screen.
> Toggle the continue arrow animation -> toggle_motion
> 01. Dialogue Basics — lines, narrator, text tags -> open_dialogue
> 02. Narration and Pacing — textspeed, wait, autodelay -> open_narration
> 03. Expressions and Characters — @character, sprites, [show]/[hide] -> open_expressions
> 04. Images and Backgrounds — @background, [bg], composition -> open_images
> More topics → -> topics_page_2
> I'm done for now -> end_early

@label toggle_motion
[if tutorial_still == true]
[jump set_motion]
[else]
[jump set_still]
[endif]

@label topics_page_2
[show lavender far_left talking]
[wait 120]
Lavender: Engine systems — transitions, audio, state, movement, branching, and animation.
> 05. Transitions and Effects — fade, crossfade, flash, shake -> open_transitions
> 06. Audio and Music — bgm, sfx, voice, fades -> open_audio
> 07. Variables and Conditions — [set], [inc], [if]/[endif] -> open_variables
> 08. Character Movement — [move], easing, @position -> open_movement
> 09. Puppeteer Timelines — parallel tracks, keyframes, camera -> open_puppeteer
> 10. Choices and Branching — >, [jump], [goto], gated choices -> open_menus
> 11. Subroutines and Flow — [call]/[return], @include, structure -> open_subroutines
> 12. Best Practices — naming, bugs, writing craft -> open_best_practices
> More topics → -> topics_page_3
> ← Back -> topics_page_1
> I'm done for now -> end_early

@label topics_page_3
[show lavender far_left talking]
[wait 120]
Lavender: Production — camera work, localization, UI customization, hybrid scenes, and shipping.
> 13. Camera and Staging — [camera pan], [camera zoom], blocking -> open_camera
> 14. Localization — text keys, locale files, translation workflow -> open_localization
> 15. UI Layout and Theme — dialogue box, menu files, style properties -> open_ui_layout
> 16. Testing and Release — validation, playtesting, release checklist -> open_testing_release
> 17. VNS and JES Together — scene push, parameters, and return flow -> open_vns_jes
> More: interfaces and plugins → -> topics_page_4
> ← Back -> topics_page_1
> ← Systems -> topics_page_2
> I'm done for now -> end_early

@label topics_page_4
[show lavender far_left talking]
Lavender: Completed ${tutorial_count} of 30 lessons. Pick a workshop.
> 18. Plugins and Pikupiku — preview, presets, authoring -> open_plugins_and_line_boil
> 19. Saves and Rollback — history, slots, persistence -> open_saves_rollback_persistence
> 20. Dialogue Surfaces — ADV, NVL, bubbles -> open_dialogue_presentation
> 21. Reactive UI and Facets — live data and return values -> open_reactive_ui_and_facets
> 22. Phone Storytelling — contacts, threads, calls -> open_phone_storytelling
> More workshops → -> topics_page_5
> ← Back -> topics_page_3
> I’m done for now -> end_early

@label topics_page_5
[show lavender far_left talking]
Lavender: Completed ${tutorial_count} of 30 lessons. Pick a workshop.
> 23. Particles and Visualizers — motion and music -> open_particles_and_visualizers
> 24. Layer Groups and Lighting — stage, focus, display slots -> open_layer_groups_and_lighting
> 25. JES Workshop — entities, input, widgets -> open_jes_entities_input_widgets
> 26. JES Worlds — tilemaps, physics, RPG and AI -> open_jes_worlds_physics_rpg
> More workshops → -> topics_page_6
> ← Back -> topics_page_4
> I’m done for now -> end_early

@label topics_page_6
[show lavender far_left talking]
Lavender: Completed ${tutorial_count} of 30 lessons. Pick a workshop.
> 27. Editor Workflows — maps, diagnostics, tooling -> open_editor_workflows
> 28. Assets and Performance — catalogs, packs, profiling -> open_assets_and_performance
> 29. Accessibility and Controls — readable, playable settings -> open_accessibility_and_controls
> 30. Extensions and Capstone — Java, plugins, shipping -> open_java_extensions_and_capstone
> ← Back -> topics_page_5
> I’m done for now -> end_early

@label open_plugins_and_line_boil
[goto T18_Plugins:start]

@label open_saves_rollback_persistence
[goto T19_Saves:start]

@label open_dialogue_presentation
[goto T20_Presentation:start]

@label open_reactive_ui_and_facets
[goto T21_Facets:start]

@label open_phone_storytelling
[goto T22_Phone:start]

@label open_particles_and_visualizers
[goto T23_Particles:start]

@label open_layer_groups_and_lighting
[goto T24_Stage:start]

@label open_jes_entities_input_widgets
[goto T25_JesTools:start]

@label open_jes_worlds_physics_rpg
[goto T26_JesWorlds:start]

@label open_editor_workflows
[goto T27_Editor:start]

@label open_assets_and_performance
[goto T28_Assets:start]

@label open_accessibility_and_controls
[goto T29_Accessibility:start]

@label open_java_extensions_and_capstone
[goto T30_Extensions:start]

@label open_dialogue
[goto {{DIALOGUE_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_narration
[goto {{NARRATION_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_expressions
[goto {{EXPRESSIONS_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_images
[goto {{IMAGES_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_transitions
[goto {{TRANSITIONS_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_audio
[goto {{AUDIO_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_variables
[goto {{VARIABLES_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_movement
[goto {{MOVEMENT_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_puppeteer
[goto {{PUPPETEER_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_menus
[goto {{MENUS_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_subroutines
[goto {{SUBROUTINES_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_best_practices
[goto {{BEST_PRACTICES_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_camera
[goto {{CAMERA_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_localization
[goto {{LOCALIZATION_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_ui_layout
[goto {{UI_LAYOUT_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_testing_release
[goto {{TESTING_RELEASE_TARGET}}:start]

@label open_vns_jes
[goto {{VNS_JES_TARGET}}:start]

@label end_early
[show lavender center talking]
[wait 160]

# ─── Progress-Aware Farewell ────────────────────────────────────
# Each lesson records completion only once, on return to this hub.
# This [if] block reacts to how many the player actually completed.

[if tutorial_count >= 30]
Lavender: You covered {b}the full workshop{/b}. You have explored story scripting, presentation, interfaces, game systems, authoring tools, extensions, and production.
Lavender: That's not a tutorial anymore — that's a toolkit. You're ready to build a full game.
[elif tutorial_count >= 15]
Lavender: Good depth — you've got the core scripting systems under your belt.
Lavender: The later workshops cover reactive interfaces, plugins, JES worlds, accessibility, and release preparation. Come back when your project reaches that stage.
[elif tutorial_count > 2]
Lavender: Solid start. You've seen how dialogue, characters, and a few engine systems work.
Lavender: The lessons you skipped aren't going anywhere. Open them when a feature comes up — they work as standalone reference, not just sequential tutorials.
[elif tutorial_count > 0]
Lavender: You dipped into one or two topics. That's fine — you know the format now.
Lavender: When you run into a syntax question while writing, jump back to the specific lesson. Each one opens with the exact command syntax you need.
[else]
Lavender: No lessons completed yet — but you've seen how the hub works.
Lavender: Each lesson is a self-contained .vns file. Open any of them directly from the editor's file browser at {b}scripts/tutorial/{/b}, or come back here and pick one from the menu.
[endif]

[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: One more thing: every tutorial file is a real, runnable .vns script. They're not read-only documentation.
Lavender: Copy code snippets into your own scenes. Add comments. Modify the practice sections. They're yours now.

narrator: To return to these tutorials later, run this project and choose {b}Open Lavender’s complete JVN workshop{/b} from the prologue.
narrator: Or open any file in {b}scripts/tutorial/{/b} directly in the editor — no need to play through the hub.

Lavender: Go build something.
[end]
